INSERT INTO `questionnaire_old` VALUES (1,1,'Provide the list of facilities covered in PCI scope: 1. Facilities in PCI scope (with detailed Address) 2. PCI related Business 3. Cardholder Data payment channel (Card present  / Card Not Present)','1','2018-11-17 00:00:00','2020-01-03 11:44:22'),(2,1,'If you are using payment application e.g.  (Payment switch) then provide below information\r\n\r\n- Name of product \r\n- Version of product \r\n- Whether payment application has been validated according to PA-DSS\r\n- PA-DSS reference number, if applicable\r\n- P2PE reference number, if applicable\r\n- Expiry date of PA-DSS validation, if applicable ','1','2018-11-17 00:00:00','2020-01-03 15:53:59'),(3,1,'Provide high level network diagram showing the overall architecture of the environment being assessed. The diagrams should identify all locations and key systems, and the boundaries between them. \r\nEnsure the diagram(s) includes the following: -    \r\n\r\nAll connections into and out of the network, including demarcation points between the cardholder data environment (CDE) and other networks/zones \r\n-    Connectivity type used for data transmission (IPSEC tunnel, SSL, SFTP etc.)\r\n-    Internal, External and DMZ network zones  with cardholder application and database systems in respective network zone OR PCI scope specific VLAN’s (as well as their locations and the boundaries between them)\r\n-    All network devices firewall, IPS, Router, VPN devices, Switches devices  as applicable\r\n-    Third party connections having cardholder data shared with','1','2018-11-17 00:00:00','2020-01-03 15:54:47'),(4,1,'Provide Inventory of  inscope servers (Windows, UNIX and Linux platform) / Network devices (Firewall, Routers, IPS/IDS, VPN, Core switch), database, data storage locations and software’s or applications used.                                                                                                                                                          Iventory should include Internal and external IP\'s, Total population, Manufacturer and model no.\r\n\r\n','1','2018-11-17 00:00:00','2020-01-03 15:55:56'),(5,1,'Provide the list of externally accessible IP addresses  included in the ASV quarterly scan.','1','2018-11-17 00:00:00','2020-01-03 15:56:32'),(6,1,'Provide Firewall, Router configuration, Azure Network Security Rules and any network change management sample reports (Recent 3 samples for each of firewall and router). \r\nRecords should include following information at minimum:    \r\n- Change approval    \r\n- Change testing for firewall, router configuration    \r\n- Change testing for network connections','1','2018-11-17 00:00:00','2020-01-03 15:57:40'),(7,1,'Provide one or more detailed diagrams (including LAN, WAN or Internet) to illustrate each communication point. \r\nDiagrams should include the following: \r\n-    All boundaries of the cardholder data environment \r\n-    Any network segmentation points which are used to reduce scope of the assessment\r\n-    Boundaries between trusted and un-trusted networks\r\n-    Wireless (if available)  and wired networks \r\n-    All other connection points applicable to the assessment\r\n-    Ensure the diagram(s) include enough detail to clearly understand how each communication point functions and is secured. (For example, the level of detail may include identifying the types of devices, device interfaces, network technologies, protocols, and security controls applicable to that communication point.)     Please include date and version number in all the Network Diagrams    Please clearly depict the PCI Scope Environment in the Diagram (Use dotted lines or Colour the area)     \r\n\r\nProvide the details on Network zones / VLAN ID (from Firewall and L3 switch config) \r\n\r\nPlease use terminology like CDE and Non-CDE or colour codes to depict the servers with and without card data within the PCI Scope Environment.\r\n','1','2018-11-17 00:00:00','2020-01-03 15:58:14'),(8,1,'Provide cardholder data flow Diagrams (DFD) showing each processes  having cardholder data processing, transmission and storage -  \r\n  \r\nIdentify all the systems involve in storage, processing and transmission of cardholder data  in DFD including the systems mentioned in cardholder data matrix  for storage of cardholder data-    Show in each step of dataflow what type of cardholder data (Name, PAN, CVV, PIN , Expiry date  etc.) transmitted, processed or stored (Note-  No storage of CVV, PIN allowed post authorization for any entity, except for Issuer with business justification)\r\n\r\nSample processes may include the cardholder data transmission, storage and processing as (if applicable)\r\nfor Banks:\r\n1.    Debit and Credit card - Issuing,  \r\n2.    ATM transaction acquiring and authorization, \r\n3.    POS transaction acquiring and authorization, \r\n4.    Online transaction acquiring and authorization, \r\n5.    Charge back and Claims Process, \r\n6.    Fraud Management Process, \r\n7.    Reconciliation and Settlement process, \r\n8.    Call Center support / IVR support Example \r\nfor BPO:\r\n1.    Data flow for Customer cardholder data transmission or processing at BPO environment \r\n2.    Data flow for Customer cardholder data received over various channels  i.e. telephone (call recording), fax, email etc.','1','2018-11-17 00:00:00','2020-01-03 16:04:40'),(9,1,'Provide documented Role and responsibilities (Teams, Groups &amp; personnel) related to firewall and router devices logical management Firewall and Router user access matrix: ','1','2018-11-17 00:00:00','2020-01-03 16:05:17'),(10,1,'Provide documentation and business justification for use of all services, protocols, and ports allowed on firewall and router, including documentation of security features implemented for those protocols considered to be insecure e.g. Telnet, FTP, SNMP, POP3, IMAP etc.\r\n','1','2018-11-17 00:00:00','2020-01-03 16:05:43'),(11,2,'ISO Lorem Ipsum is simply d